./" Manpage for mmcv 
.TH man 1 "26 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	mmcv - mkdir directory, mv a file there, cd there, then edit the file in vim
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mmcv source destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	makes a directory, moves a file there, cds to wherever it is now, then edits the file in vim
.br
	only edits the last file if you give multiple
.SH OPTIONS
	mv default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose
.br
	mkdir and vim default options do not work
.SH EXAMPLES
	mmcv hi.csv csvs
.br
	mmcv sdifji.py ../../ijsdif
.SH BUGS
	probably none
